# `usp_Get_Rental_Inquiry_Details` (client, TKTS-926): add to your existing client classes

Input: `p_Session_Key`, `p_Location_Function_Id`, `p_Rental_Inquiry_Id`, `p_Rental_Booking_Id`. Output: `p_Result_Code`, plus one row.
- Booking id is null: the row comes from `Rental_Inquiry` (first time the inquiry is opened).
- Booking id is set: the row comes from `Rental_Booking`, with `Rental_Booking_Id`, `Rental_Notes` and `Contract_Attachment` added.

Endpoint: `POST /api/v1/rental-amenities/inquiries/details`

## Timezone handling
The DB values are UTC: `Rental_Start_At`, `Rental_End_At`, `Recieved_Inquiry_At` (the proc spells it "Recieved") and `Last_Updated`.
**This proc does not return a timezone.** The previous list API (`usp_Get_Rental_Inquiries`) does return one per row,
so the UI sends that same `timezone` back in this request. It is validated and used to convert the four values to local time.
`Last_Updated` can be NULL (inquiry branch), so every date is null-checked.

