### 4. RentalAmenityService
Imports: `java.time.LocalDateTime`, `java.util.List`, `java.util.Map` (plus your existing `TimezoneConverter`).
```java
@Override
public Map<String, Object> getRentalInquiryDetails(TicketRequest req) {
    // Throws ValidationException for a null/blank/invalid IANA timezone
    TimezoneConverter.validateTimezone(req.getTimezone());

    List<Map<String, Object>> rows = rentalAmenityDao.getRentalInquiryDetails(req);
    if (rows.isEmpty()) {
        return null;
    }

    Map<String, Object> row = rows.get(0);
    for (String key : List.of("rentalStartAt", "rentalEndAt", "recievedInquiryAt", "lastUpdated")) {
        if (row.get(key) != null) {
            row.put(key, TimezoneConverter.toLocal((LocalDateTime) row.get(key), req.getTimezone()));
        }
    }
    return row;
}
```
The key `recievedInquiryAt` keeps the proc's spelling ("Recieved_Inquiry_At"). If the DB team fixes it, change it here too.
No `@Transactional` is needed because this is a read-only call.

