## Check in the stored procedure
- The permission check calls `sys_Check_Session_Permission(p_Session_Key, @Location_Function_Id, ...)`. That variable is never set from the
  parameter `p_Location_Function_Id`. The same mistake was in `usp_Get_Rental_Inquiries`. The Jira comment says the proc has been tested, so it may be
  a misread in my screenshot, but please check it.
- The inquiry branch selects `Rental_Start_At` and `Rental_End_At` from `Rental_Inquiry`. Earlier, the `Rental_Inquiry` table showed `Event_Start_At` and `Event_End_At`.
  If the table was renamed, no problem. If not, that branch will fail.
- The two branches return different columns: only the booking branch has `Rental_Booking_Id`, `Rental_Notes` and `Contract_Attachment`.
  The UI has to handle those being missing for an inquiry that has no booking yet.
